#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# every

#% text
# `every(xs, p)` gives `true` when `p(x)` is `true` for every element `x` of `xs`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
every([2, 4, 6], is_even)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
every([2, 3, 6], is_even)
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# An empty list satisfies every test:

#% cell
every([], is_even)
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `some`, `all_true`, `select`
